I see what you mean. I'm only checking if any one digit works. I should check if any digit *fails* and then decide. Try this:

def find_nums(start, end):
    res = []
    for n in range(start, end + 1):
        possible = True
        for digit in str(n):
            if n % int(digit) != 0:
                possible = False
                break
        if possible:
            res.append(n)
    return res

